{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be","id":1454585,"title":"What would you want to be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-09T09:13:52-07:00","id":1454585,"title":"What would you want to be?","content":"Now with the information for Adventure! out, at least for the backers, what would you prefer to be in the Trinity Continuum? Psion, Nova, Talent, etc.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd probably either want to be a Darkstar Nova with the equivalent of a Mega-Attribute dot in every Attribute plus a couple of useful Mega-Edges or a Vitakinetic Psion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T09:33:54-07:00","id":1454586,"title":"","content":"Talent all the way. Luck manipulation to have things go my way? Hello door to opportunity and a comfortable life!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T09:39:42-07:00","id":1454588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JeffreyBezos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1454586#post1454586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talent all the way. Luck manipulation to have things go my way? Hello door to opportunity and a comfortable life!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same here, I'm team talent. Psychic powers and Quantum powers are cool and all, but luck is the only thing that requires no skill, which comes very handy if you're not smart. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 07-09-2021, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T11:12:10-07:00","id":1454590,"title":"","content":"Probably a nova. Super powers would be great, and I'm lazy enough I'm not going to be gathering Flux too quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T11:45:23-07:00","id":1454592,"title":"","content":"I think a psiad would provide the most interesting taste of the universe- the sheer power isn't there, but the breadth of experience is. And with one dot in vitakinesis, you might have a long, long time to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T11:48:24-07:00","id":1454593,"title":"","content":"For me a nova would be my first choice, probably a Darkstar nova like someone already said I think it's a good starting point for a nova. If this was aberrant setting as a nova first things I would learn are dormancy and chrysalis to keep transcendence down to minimum, then I would join daedalus league so that If things do go badly I can go offworld. I would prioritise getting mega stamina 6 to have endless lifespan but apart from that not sure what I would specialise in or just have a quite broad power range at low dots.<br /> <br /> If I couldn't be a nova I would probably be a psiad not a Psion as psiads are more flexible and versatile, I would like the powers that allow for eternal youth and perfect health I'm not sure what modes they are I think it's vitakinetic but could someone correct me. The extra lifespan would give the time to develop my abilities as think it's said pauses take a while train the modes?. In setting would definitely keep a low profile because psiads aren't as powerful as other types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-09T18:40:15-07:00","id":1454628,"title":"","content":"I gotta go with Talent. But Psiad is a CLOSE second. Talents can do, well, pretty much anything up to and including manipulating reality to have things go their way. But Psiads? Well, I am using a Psiad antagonist in my Aberrant game and the character is scary as hell...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T12:29:20-07:00","id":1454701,"title":"","content":"While the raw power of Novas is tempting, the inevitable slide into corruption is not.<br /> If I could be any TC template, I'd want to be a Psion with Teleportation and an Aux Mode in Psycholocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T21:21:40-07:00","id":1454719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1454701#post1454701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the raw power of Novas is tempting, the inevitable slide into corruption is not.<br /> If I could be any TC template, I'd want to be a Psion with Teleportation and an Aux Mode in Psycholocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair to Novas, corruption isn't inevitable, but can become likely for those who get too drunk on their power.<br /> <br /> That would be a good Psion powerset though, would be fun and freeing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T21:53:46-07:00","id":1454720,"title":"","content":"Nova. The sheer power and versatility are just too good to pass up if I had to choose. (You can get pretty damned strong without Flux getting out of hand, but I'd be willing to put up with some Transcendance.)<br /> <br /> I guess I would (given the choice) probably go the &quot;dark star&quot; route as well to start with, and (slowly!) branch out into new quantum abilities from there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T23:01:21-07:00","id":1454721,"title":"","content":"To those who chose Darkstar Nova: why not a &quot;normal&quot; Nova?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T03:08:30-07:00","id":1454727,"title":"","content":"Dark star nova\u2019s tend to start with no transcendance is one reason for me. For those who don\u2019t know what a dark star nova is, it\u2019s a nova that tends to be at the lower end of the power scale but tend to have mega stats in many if not all areas, they aren\u2019t always overtly nova or superhuman and sometimes get away with being a very gifted baseline. I would say they are less likely to get drunk on their power and have a good foundation to develop from.<br /> <br /> Think maybe something like captain america maybe a bit higher level but with enhanced intelligence as well.<br /> <br /> Another reason for me is that I find alot of novas in my opinion seem to have narrow focus when it comes to their powers which I dislike in the characters that I make. I like a my swiss army novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26058,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","user":"Aeonstorm","date":". 07-12-2021, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T05:35:57-07:00","id":1454735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1454721#post1454721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To those who chose Darkstar Nova: why not a &quot;normal&quot; Nova?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'm not very good at a lot of stuff, and I would like to be decent at all that stuff more than I would like to fly around and shoot energy blasts.<br /> <br /> If novas were stuck with only their starting powers and could never expand from there, I might have chosen differently. But I could always learn to fly later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T17:42:05-07:00","id":1454775,"title":"","content":"Just speaking personally, for me transcendence would be unavoidable. Not because I'd abuse my powers or rush to evolution, but because you gain quantum flux whenever you botch a quantum power check. And the number of times I have messed up things like Shaving, Clipping my Toenails, Walking, and Brushing My Teeth badly enough to draw non-trivial amounts of blood tells me that if I had access to any Quantum powers, I WOULD rack up flux faster than I could possibly shed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T19:27:54-07:00","id":1454778,"title":"","content":"If node brains are still a thing in Aberrant, I'd prefer to be a Nova. I'd prefer to start with healing and empathic powers. (But also a bit of super strength, force fields, and super constitution, so I can protect my patients if need be).<br /> <br /> Maybe I could can myself Gawain after Arthur's nephew who was &quot;the best chirgeon in the world.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T19:35:05-07:00","id":1454779,"title":"","content":"Not sure what you mean by &quot;node brains&quot;, since Nodes are no longer a thing; but mental Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T23:34:44-07:00","id":1454800,"title":"","content":"Full nova. No question. I care nothing for transcendence, inevitable or not. I'll bury the corpse of this tawdry and broken human existence and then shit on the grave. So I'm separated from society by my very alien-ness? So what? That's no different from what I have right now. I won't miss what I never had in the first place. While you're all busy trying to fit in, or keep hold of something you should be growing out of, I'll be studying THE UNIVERSE. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T02:19:30-07:00","id":1454805,"title":"","content":"Definitely a Nova focused on Mega-Attributes (so, Dark Star-ish early on, but I wouldn't want to stay that way). Being just flatly better at everything? Hell yes I want that. Transcendence is an issue, sure, but not an insurmountable one, and the power to change the world for the better is pretty enticing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T03:49:04-07:00","id":1454808,"title":"","content":"High PSI Psiad with a smathering of Teleportation, Vitakinesis and maybe some Clairvoyance and Quantakinesis - and Mindshare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T05:21:34-07:00","id":1454815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1454800#post1454800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full nova. No question. I care nothing for transcendence, inevitable or not. I'll bury the corpse of this tawdry and broken human existence and then shit on the grave. So I'm separated from society by my very alien-ness? So what? That's no different from what I have right now. I won't miss what I never had in the first place. While you're all busy trying to fit in, or keep hold of something you should be growing out of, I'll be studying THE UNIVERSE. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree, when the aberrant war comes about and novas find out that baselines didn't ever really trust them due to medusa protocols or whatever your using in your story, I don't understand why the nova's didn't just say you don't want our help (basically fixed planet and problems caused by baselines) fine we'll leave. Then they go off into space and make a super advanced civilisation not burdened by those left on earth who were jealous.<br /> <br /> The way I see it a nova who has a few decades of experience with his powers even if he's been careful and not rushing or developing flux can do amazing things. I imagine a group of them going off into space with those loyal to them could end up building stuff like Dyson spheres or matrioshka brains and making galactic empire in another galaxy.<br /> <br /> another reason I would choose nova.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T08:01:33-07:00","id":1454824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1454779#post1454779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what you mean by &amp;quot;node brains&amp;quot;, since Nodes are no longer a thing; but mental Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges are.</div> </div> </div> </div>In first edition, second generation Novas didn't have a separate Node. The traits of the Node were distributed throughout the Nova's whole brain. This would slow and provide resistance to Taint. Basically, I wanted a trait that allows me to have and use Nova powers while gaining very little Transcendence if any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T08:09:39-07:00","id":1454825,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. I prefer the Talents out of all of the various types, particularly the &quot;Weird Science&quot; types, who might be every bit as potent as all but the mightiest Novas. But for myself, I would want to be a Nova allied with the Daedalus League. Heading out to distant worlds, setting up colonies and such is so very appealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T09:26:41-07:00","id":1454836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1454824#post1454824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In first edition, second generation Novas didn't have a separate Node. The traits of the Node were distributed throughout the Nova's whole brain. This would slow and provide resistance to Taint. Basically, I wanted a trait that allows me to have and use Nova powers while gaining very little Transcendence if any.</div> </div> </div> </div>In TC:Ab, the notion of MR Nodes has been replaced by MR Coils, which are distributed throughout the Nova's body. The official rules don't have anything to the effect of preventing Quantum-induced Transcendence; though if you put the work into Grounding any Flux you acquire, you can prevent any Flux-induced Transcendence. That said, see the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454210-avoiding-transcendence\">Avoiding Transcendence</a> hack linked to in my signature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-13-2021, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T09:26:49-07:00","id":1454837,"title":"","content":"I LOVE that the Deadalus League is a major faction now, it's probably my favorite for 2nd edition. I'd have been a terat in 1st edition that existed as a semi-hermit on earth before the aberrant war and the idiocy of human insecurity forced me off world. But now, I'd already be exploring the whole of the galaxy with the most broad-minded of humanity leaving the rest to fight over their egos and/or piles of dirt and propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T10:07:20-07:00","id":1454841,"title":"","content":"Full Nova. I don't have any trouble bonding with a dog now, I don't forsee any huge problems arising from transcendence... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-13T12:08:44-07:00","id":1454848,"title":"","content":"For me, a daredevil \u2014 or the &quot;deliberate daredevils&quot; that TC:A! hints at in a parallel timeline to TC:Ab, where the Doyen shield stays up and Talents eventually learn how to consciously manipulate the timeline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-24T01:18:12-07:00","id":1455493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1454837#post1454837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I LOVE that the Deadalus League is a major faction now, it's probably my favorite for 2nd edition. I'd have been a terat in 1st edition that existed as a semi-hermit on earth before the aberrant war and the idiocy of human insecurity forced me off world. But now, I'd already be exploring the whole of the galaxy with the most broad-minded of humanity leaving the rest to fight over their egos and/or piles of dirt and propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, of all the Players Guide factions, the Daedalus League (which now seems to be mashed together a bit with the Protectors) was easily my favorite, although I wouldn't mind seeing more about City Protectors, the Gestalt (the barely mentioned psychic order, which I imagine to be crawling with psiads as well as 'psychic' Novas) and City Protectors and various national teams (like Nordselyne, Nippontai, Column Shiva and the Exploding Heavenly Mandate). Do not miss the focus on the Cult of Ashtaroth or, to a lesser extent, the XWF (who were at least delightfully over the top).<br /> <br /> A Daedalus League spin-off faction that concentrates on exploring and developing hostile zones *on Earth* (such as an undersea habitat, or one in Antarctica, or one deep in the crust) could be interesting, as well, and also tie in somehow to future-Earth develop of undersea habitats, or Adventure!-era ties to the 'Hollow Earth' or even the Protectors former base in Antarctica and the future Amundsen City of the Aeon era.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T08:36:38-08:00","id":1468348,"title":"","content":"I note that the power no longer exists in the Onyx Path version of Aberrant, but my first choice would be a Temporal Manipulator. It opens the doors to all kinds of other powers. (Healing, self and others, Precognition, Time Dilation, shimmer, disintegration, repair), and that's all before reaching levels of Cross Time Travel and Time Warp <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27178-leighmonroe","name":"Leighmonroe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T08:48:30-08:00","id":1468349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leighmonroe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1468348#post1468348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I note that the power no longer exists in the Onyx Path version of Aberrant, but my first choice would be a Temporal Manipulator. It opens the doors to all kinds of other powers. (Healing, self and others, Precognition, Time Dilation, shimmer, disintegration, repair), and that's all before reaching levels of Cross Time Travel and Time Warp <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>In defense of the new system, Temporal Manipulation is hinted as Elemental Mastery: Time, and all the options you described would work fine as techniques of that.<br /> <br /> Crosstime Travel and Time Warp are too much of plot devices to be left in the characters hand indiscriminately. But if you really want to run this kind of power, I would suggest to use it as Power Stunts, what you\u2019d imply a long term cost to the character (gaining flux), and so not be used \u201cfreely\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T09:10:06-08:00","id":1468351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1468349#post1468349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In defense of the new system, Temporal Manipulation is hinted as Elemental Mastery: Time, and all the options you described would work fine as techniques of that.<br /> <br /> Crosstime Travel and Time Warp are too much of plot devices to be left in the characters hand indiscriminately. But if you really want to run this kind of power, I would suggest to use it as Power Stunts, what you\u2019d imply a long term cost to the character (gaining flux), and so not be used \u201cfreely\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In a game setting I would agree that Time Warp and Cross Time Travel are too powerful, but hey the question was what would we want to be, not what would we want to play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27178-leighmonroe","name":"Leighmonroe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T10:24:02-08:00","id":1468355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leighmonroe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1468351#post1468351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In a game setting I would agree that Time Warp and Cross Time Travel are too powerful, but hey the question was what would we want to be, not what would we want to play. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed\u2026 so nice pick!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-19T11:41:36-08:00","id":1468362,"title":"","content":"Biokinetic psion. I've always been fascinated with shapeshifters, and I love that the change of the Norca between editions went from amoral spies/assassins/drug dealers to straight up Zorro/Batman/James Bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25998-loneshark","name":"Loneshark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T10:59:53-08:00","id":1468412,"title":"","content":"I feel like Nova is really appealing and less risky then what the official timeline of the Trinity Continuum would leave you to believe but I'd still wouldn't want to go that root. I'd go Psiad with Vitakinesis and Biokinesis. I feel like that is a good mix of general utility to make my life more comfortable and enjoyable and the easy low hanging fruit that lets me immediately start making a positive difference in the world while still having a lot of room for long term growth. Also as a Psiad I'm still not locked out of the other Aptitudes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T03:08:53-08:00","id":1468477,"title":"","content":"For me, it has to be nova. It's the sole path that allows you as an individual to go from human, to hero, to god, to transcending reality altogether. Yeah, there are risks, as there are with anything having a big pay-off... but to go from me now and grow beyond our reality over centuries of growth, exploration, and change? Yeah that beats lucky hero and even &quot;safe&quot; psion easily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1454836#post1454836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In TC:Ab, the notion of MR Nodes has been replaced by MR Coils, which are distributed throughout the Nova's body.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, MR coils were around in the 1st edition. I don't think they've replaced nodes so much as merely deleted nodes as a concept. Nodes governed how much Quantum could be channelled per turn and how quickly you recovered it. Made it somewhat of a &quot;must have&quot; merit in the rules too. No real explanation of MR coils replacing that in core boo, though there may be an expansion I've missed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T07:05:23-08:00","id":1468494,"title":"","content":"No. The MR node was a portion of your brain that let you control the quantum forces. That has been replaced by MR coils that just exist in your cellular structure. The Merit let you control more Quantum per turn but every Nova in 1E had a MR node.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T07:07:45-08:00","id":1468495,"title":"","content":"There was a reference to MR could in 1e in that Kikjak interview comic (page 26), but that\u2019s all. So, yes there were MR Coils, but there was no other references to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-21-2021, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T20:27:49-08:00","id":1468557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1468494#post1468494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. The MR node was a portion of your brain that let you control the quantum forces. That has been replaced by MR coils that just exist in your cellular structure. The Merit let you control more Quantum per turn but every Nova in 1E had a MR node.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what the MR node was in 1e, and that every nova had one, but the <b>concept</b> (both in lore &amp; mechanically) of the node was that the larger / more developed it was, the more Quantum they could <b><i>channel per turn</i></b> and the quicker they could <b><i>recover Quantum</i></b>. This was independent of the nova's Quantum Trait which, amongst other things, controlled the Quantum pool <i><b>size</b>.</i> MR coils are mentioned in the lore (as Mateus mentioned) in the interview with Kijack amongst all the world background stuff at the start of the 1e core rulebook. They are, according to that interview, used to channel quantum in the novas' body and apparently why novas are more resilient than baselines though the explanation is... not great. Seriously, it gave me a headache back when I first played it in university some twenty years ago.<br /> <br /> In 2e, they mention MR coils exist &amp; can be detected, but what they are and what they do has been left VERY vague. The only things we know about MR coils is they exist (&amp; can be detected), they're named after the people that discovered them, and they're used to make Mite. That's it. They might go into more details on that (or maybe have outside the Aberrant specific books - I don't have all the Aeon books). More importantly, as a <i><b>concept</b></i> there is no longer any differentiation between a nova's Quantum rating, their pool size, and their recovery rates. You get a fixed pool based on Quantum, you recover half of that pool between scenes at rest (or not at rest for a point of Flux), and you can recover the entire pool (no matter it's size) for a point of Flux if you rest between scenes. There is no explicit concept of how much Quantum you can spend during a turn at all, outside the restrictions imposed by the amount you have and the number of actions/powers you can use on your turn.<br /> <br /> I agree, given MR coils are used to make Mite, that they must have something to do with channelling Quantum in a nova... but the lore is very vague on the matter. I suspect if we query the devs on the specifics, we'll be given a <i>&quot;whatever works for your table&quot;</i> style answer. \ud83e\udd23","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T04:29:36-08:00","id":1468580,"title":"","content":"MR coils exist, and do not exist in non-novas.<br /> <br /> But <i>not</i> finding MR coils does not necessarily indicate that someone is not a nova. While the presence of coils is a good indicator that someone is a nova, it's not definitive. It could be that the coils are in a different part of that nova's physiology -- you're testing blood, but it's in the cell walls of the nova's organs instead, for example -- or it could be that MR coils are created through an external stressor that is unrelated to eruption. There's no tricorder-like scanning device (yet) that can tell if you've got MR coils, docs can only test individual samples.<br /> <br /> Or it could be that the non-coiled novas they're testing aren't novas at all, but rather psiads.<br /> <br /> The common theory has it that coils assist in channelling quantum, but due to the above factors and the science being in its infancy, it's hard to tell for sure.<br /> <br /> As Eternl Knight says, whatever works for your table. We've left it open to interpretation on purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":".  samples 11-22-2021, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T05:29:38-08:00","id":1468582,"title":"","content":"And that's before you get into the confusion of when Novas turn into inorganic substances.<br /> <br /> I know Onyx Path has limits into how many potential books get funded but one of my favorite parts of the original was it going into Nova physiology and I personally would love a source book or at least a section dedicated in this new one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T05:31:33-08:00","id":1468583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stanlemon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1454585-what-would-you-want-to-be?p=1468582#post1468582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's before you get into the confusion of when Novas turn into inorganic substances.<br /> <br /> I know Onyx Path has limits into how many potential books get funded but one of my favorite parts of the original was it going into Nova physiology and I personally would love a source book or at least a section dedicated in this new one</div> </div> </div> </div>Write one! I am sure people would love to see what you think about it. Nexus is here for that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>